eady says who decided D-16 and gives the tasks, sample sizes and acceptance numbers, and the start gate for T-UX-01 is enforced by tests. The view-model contract already exists as JSON Schema with generated Dart and TS clients, so screens can only use fields the contract defines. I6 is a property of the API response (every amount carries a source, and a broken chain gives data_missing), so the right place to test it is T-AP-02, not the screens. The one real gap is the two pending axes on Amount: until they are promoted, T-AP-02 cannot fully check its done criteria. Not critical because this is a reversible documentation and sequencing decision with no money, credentials, legal or production impact.\n\n**Options:** [\'A (chosen): Treat D-16 and the L8 contract as already settled by DEC-D-16 and packages/schemas. Keep I6 testing in T-AP-02 and follow up only on the two pending Amount axes.\', \'B: Write a new D-16 proposal. Rejected because DEC-D-16 already has tasks, sample sizes and thresholds, and a duplicate record would conflict with it.\', \'C: Add a separate task to freeze an L8 view-model contract before any screen work. Rejected because the T-CT-01/03 outputs already contain the view-model schemas and generated clients, so this would redo finished work.\', "D: Start a Flutter or Next.js scaffold now to close the \'zero code\' part. Rejected because T-MB-01 is gated by its stage and dependencies, and empty scaffolds would add no I6 evidence."]\n\n**Revisit if:** The owner overrides the DEC-D-16 thresholds or sample sizes; T-AP-02 starts while evidence_kind or applicability are still pending; a screen task needs a view-model field missing from packages/schemas; T-MB-02 is allowed to start before T-AP-02\'s I6 contract test exists; or the stage plan moves app or web work earlier.\n'

